 "why_fp32_ir_is_not_bit_identical_to_torch": "the CPU plugin picks its own execution precision. precision_hint_ab runs the SAME FP32 IR twice -- once at the plugin default, once with INFERENCE_PRECISION_HINT=f32 -- so the drift is attributed by measurement rather than by assertion. Each variant above records the execution precision it was checked at.",
